Give it to me.

6
00:00:15,265 --> 00:00:17,893
Is it me or does it smell like updog in here?

7
00:00:17,976 --> 00:00:19,061
What's "updog"?

8
00:00:19,144 --> 00:00:20,979
Nothing much, what's up with you?

9
00:00:22,314 --> 00:00:26,485
Oh, wow. I walked right into that.

10
00:00:26,818 --> 00:00:28,654
Oh, that's brilliant.

11
00:00:29,321 --> 00:00:31,448
Hey, Stanley, is that jacket made of updog?

12
00:00:31,532 --> 00:00:32,783
I'm on the phone.

13
00:00:37,621 --> 00:00:39,414
What flavor coffee is that? Updog?

14
00:00:39,498 --> 00:00:40,541
What's that?

15
00:00:40,624 --> 00:00:43,126
I don't know. Nothing, what's up with you?

16
00:00:43,961 --> 00:00:46,129
Huh? No, damn it.

17
00:00:46,421 --> 00:00:47,589
What does that mean?

18
00:00:47,673 --> 00:00:48,840
What does what mean?

19
00:00:48,924 --> 00:00:51,426
That thing you just said. Just forget it.

20
00:00:51,802 --> 00:00:52,803
Dwight!

21
00:00:53,595 --> 00:00:56,932
Hey, is it me, or does this place smell like updog?

22
00:00:57,015 --> 00:01:01,311
What's "updog"? Gotcha! Oh, God.

23
00:01:01,687 --> 00:01:02,896
Crap.

24
00:01:05,148 --> 00:01:07,359
Nothing. How are you doing?

25
00:01:08,026 --> 00:01:09,152
Good.

26
00:01:09,361 --> 00:01:10,779
How are you doing?

27
00:01:15,951 --> 00:01:16,952
Damn it!

28
00:01:53,280 --> 00:01:55,866
<i>Today is spring cleaning day here at Dunder Mifflin.</i>

29
00:01:55,949 --> 00:01:58,702
<i>And yes, I know it's January. I am not an idiot.</i>

30
00:01:58,785 --> 00:02:01,371
<i>But, if you do your spring cleaning in January,</i>

31
00:02:01,455 --> 00:02:04,124
guess what you don't have to do in the spring!

32
00:02:04,249 --> 00:02:05,417
Anything.

33
00:02:05,917 --> 00:02:08,378
They say a cluttered desk means a cluttered mind.

34
00:02:08,462 --> 00:02:12,132
Well, I say an empty desk means an... Empty mind.

35
00:02:12,215 --> 00:02:15,260
No, that's not... No, that's not what I was gonna say.

36
00:02:15,719 --> 00:02:17,304
Meredith, the men's room.

37
00:02:17,387 --> 00:02:20,807
Make sure you replace the urinal cakes, they're worn down.

38
00:02:20,891 --> 00:02:23,518
Kevin, file drawers.

39
00:02:24,227 --> 00:02:27,022
Angela, kitchen. Oscar, dusting.

40
00:02:27,105 --> 00:02:29,524
Where is Oscar? He's out sick.

41
00:02:30,651 --> 00:02:33,779
That's unacceptable. I agree. It's unacceptable.

42
00:02:39,117 --> 00:02:41,119
What are you guys doing?

43
00:02:43,121 --> 00:02:44,665
Michael? Yes?

44
00:02:47,751 --> 00:02:49,670
Oscar is out sick.

45
00:02:50,754 --> 00:02:52,422
On a Friday?

46
00:02:58,011 --> 00:03:00,055
Can I do some of the talking? I will do the talking.

47
00:03:00,138 --> 00:03:01,658
Okay, let him know that I'm here. - <i>Hello?</i>

48
00:03:01,682 --> 00:03:03,602
What difference does it make whether you're here?

49
00:03:03,684 --> 00:03:06,186
<i>Hello?</i> Hi, Oscar, it's Michael.

50
00:03:06,353 --> 00:03:07,521
And Dwight.

51
00:03:07,771 --> 00:03:09,940
Yeah. Heard you were under the weather?

52
00:03:10,023 --> 00:03:11,900
<i>Yeah, I think I came down with the flu.</i>

53
00:03:11,983 --> 00:03:14,403
Really? Oh, that is a shame.

54
00:03:14,486 --> 00:03:16,571
You know it's cleaning day here today.

55
00:03:16,655 --> 00:03:19,199
Could've used some of that famous Hispanic cleaning ethic.

56
00:03:19,282 --> 00:03:20,742
<i>Yeah, I feel terrible about it.</i>

57
00:03:20,826 --> 00:03:22,828
Ask him his symptoms, I'm on WebMD.

58
00:03:22,911 --> 00:03:24,246
What are your symptoms?

59
00:03:24,329 --> 00:03:26,164
<i>I have the chills.</i>

60
00:03:26,248 --> 00:03:28,917
<i>I'm feeling nauseous, and my head's killing.</i>

61
00:03:31,878 --> 00:03:32,879
Checks out.

62
00:03:32,963 --> 00:03:34,683
<i>Michael, is there anything you need from me?</i>

63
00:03:34,715 --> 00:03:37,134
<i>I'd like to go back to bed.</i> I need you to go to bed.

64
00:03:37,217 --> 00:03:40,220
I need you to get better. See you Monday, unless you're still sick.

65
00:03:40,303 --> 00:03:41,555
So have a great long weekend.

66
00:03:41,638 --> 00:03:43,265
<i>I'll just be sleep...</i>

67
00:03:44,599 --> 00:03:47,436
Okay, first impressions. He sounded sick.

68
00:03:47,519 --> 00:03:49,271
Which is exactly how you'd want to sound,

69
00:03:49,354 --> 00:03:51,082
if you wanted someone to think you were sick.

70
00:03:51,106 --> 00:03:52,333
That's exactly what I was thinking.

71
00:03:52,357 --> 00:03:54,735
Question. May I investigate? Yeah.

72
00:03:54,818 --> 00:03:57,487
Drop what you're doing. Make this a priority.

73
00:03:58,071 --> 00:04:00,615
Because an office can't function efficiently

74
00:04:00,699 --> 00:04:03,952
unless people are at their desks, doing their jobs.

75
00:04:04,244 --> 00:04:05,287
I bought my veil.

76
00:04:05,370 --> 00:04:07,539
Oh, my God, that is so exciting!

77
00:04:07,831 --> 00:04:09,416
Can I be a bridesmaid?

78
00:04:10,667 --> 00:04:13,712
Listen, you don't have to answer now, but how are you going to do your hair?

79
00:04:13,795 --> 00:04:16,381
Okay, I was thinking about wearing it down.

80
00:04:17,048 --> 00:04:20,927
Kind of like, I don't know, like, loose with big curls?

81
00:04:21,052 --> 00:04:23,555
You look like an angel. I'm seriously gonna cry.

82
00:04:23,638 --> 00:04:26,767
Wowey! Mikey likey!

83
00:04:26,850 --> 00:04:30,687
Why don't you wear your hair like that all the time? It's much sexier.

84
00:04:32,981 --> 00:04:35,150
Man, this must be torture for you.

85
00:04:37,152 --> 00:04:38,528
Yeah, on the booze cruise,

86
00:04:38,612 --> 00:04:42,282
I told Michael about some feelings I used to have for Pam.

87
00:04:43,116 --> 00:04:46,953
I had just broken up with Katy, and had a couple of drinks,

88
00:04:47,037 --> 00:04:51,082
and I confided in the world's worst confidante.

89
00:04:56,087 --> 00:04:58,381
- Hey, Michael. - Hey, Jim-bag!

90
00:05:00,050 --> 00:05:03,136
Remember that thing I told you on the booze cruise about Pam?

91
00:05:03,220 --> 00:05:05,514
That was personal.

92
00:05:05,889 --> 00:05:08,892
So if we could just keep that between you and me, that would be great.

93
00:05:08,975 --> 00:05:11,102
Really? Who else knows?

94
00:05:11,186 --> 00:05:12,354
Nobody.

95
00:05:12,729 --> 00:05:13,897
Wow.

96
00:05:14,648 --> 00:05:19,236
Jim and I are great friends. We hang out a ton, mostly at work.

97
00:05:19,736 --> 00:05:22,405
But the fact that he told me his secret and no one else

98
00:05:22,489 --> 00:05:24,783
says everything about our friendship.

99
00:05:25,242 --> 00:05:30,163
And it is why I intend on keeping that secret for as long as I possibly can.

100
00:05:31,581 --> 00:05:32,666
My lips are sealed.

101
00:05:32,749 --> 00:05:33,834
<i>My lips are sealed</i>

102
00:05:33,917 --> 00:05:36,336
Bangles. All right. Great. Thank you.

103
00:05:36,419 --> 00:05:38,505
<i>Can you hear me?</i>

104
00:05:39,005 --> 00:05:42,467
<i>They talk about us Telling lies</i>

105
00:05:42,634 --> 00:05:47,138
Listen, temp. I'm conducting a little investigation.

106
00:05:47,222 --> 00:05:50,433
So, I'm no longer gonna be able to head up spring cleaning.

107
00:05:50,517 --> 00:05:51,893
Do you think you can handle it?

108
00:05:51,977 --> 00:05:53,436
Yeah, I think I can handle it.

109
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:56,314
Do you think, or do you know?

110
00:05:57,107 --> 00:05:58,316
I think.

111
00:06:01,069 --> 00:06:03,113
Oh, God. Here.

112
00:06:06,241 --> 00:06:08,952
Hey, what you getting? I'm going with grape.

113
00:06:09,035 --> 00:06:11,830
Good stuff. Good stuff.

114
00:06:12,998 --> 00:06:14,624
Did you see the game last night?

115
00:06:14,708 --> 00:06:15,750
Which game?

116
00:06:16,084 --> 00:06:17,294
Any of them.

117
00:06:20,005 --> 00:06:24,551
So, what's the 411? Any updates on the "P" situation?

118
00:06:24,676 --> 00:06:26,678
I don't know any... P-A-M.

119
00:06:26,761 --> 00:06:28,847
P-A-M. Yeah. Oh, okay.

120
00:06:28,930 --> 00:06:31,391
No, it's okay, we're talking code. What is?

121
00:06:31,474 --> 00:06:34,519
Listen, Stan, you know, how long does it take for you to pick out a soda?

122
00:06:34,603 --> 00:06:38,148
I'm gonna take off, actually. All right, well, cool.

123
00:06:40,150 --> 00:06:41,484
Still deciding?

124
00:06:44,237 --> 00:06:48,408
Peach ice tea. You're gonna hate it.

125
00:06:48,783 --> 00:06:51,620
Hey, Oscar. How you doing? Dwight Schrute calling.

126
00:06:51,745 --> 00:06:53,538
Listen, little question for you, buddy.

127
00:06:53,622 --> 00:06:56,750
I called six minutes ago and no one answered.

128
00:06:56,833 --> 00:06:59,336
So, I was wondering if you could explain...

129
00:06:59,419 --> 00:07:04,215
Oh, I see. So, sounds like you're too sick to come into work,

130
00:07:04,299 --> 00:07:06,426
but you're well enough to go to the pharmacy.

131
00:07:06,509 --> 00:07:09,763
There are several different ways to tell if a perp is lying.

132
00:07:09,846 --> 00:07:12,515
The liar will avoid direct eye contact.

133
00:07:13,308 --> 00:07:17,062
The liar will cover part of his or her face with his hand,

134
00:07:17,145 --> 00:07:18,271
especially the mouth.

135
00:07:19,439 --> 00:07:21,066
The liar will perspire.

136
00:07:22,943 --> 00:07:26,905
Unfortunately, I spoke to Oscar on the phone so none of this is useful.

137
00:07:32,035 --> 00:07:34,996
It's grape! Soda!

138
00:07:35,288 --> 00:07:36,539
Tony the Tiger. Yeah.

139
00:07:36,623 --> 00:07:38,750
You don't hear that much anymore. Not so much.

140
00:07:38,833 --> 00:07:40,669
Okay, what is going on here?

141
00:07:41,211 --> 00:07:43,546
Nothing. Oh, really, nothing?

142
00:07:44,005 --> 00:07:46,841
Fact. You are drinking grape soda, you never drink grape soda.

143
00:07:46,925 --> 00:07:49,803
Fact. You are talking to Jim, you never talk to Jim.

144
00:07:49,886 --> 00:07:52,389
Fact. I love grape soda, I always have.

145
00:07:52,472 --> 00:07:56,226
Fact. Jim and I talk all the time. We tell each other secrets.

146
00:07:56,518 --> 00:07:58,895
Okay, so what is the secret, Michael? Look, I...

147
00:07:58,979 --> 00:08:02,232
I had asked Michael if I could head up the Oscar investigation.

148
00:08:02,315 --> 00:08:04,275
And he said that only Dwight

149
00:08:04,359 --> 00:08:07,904
was capable of handling such sensitive material.

150
00:08:10,615 --> 00:08:11,866
Is that true?

151
00:08:15,412 --> 00:08:20,333
I don't know. Yeah, yeah, yeah. It is.

152
00:08:20,959 --> 00:08:22,419
Thank you, Michael.

153
00:08:23,003 --> 00:08:24,879
I know you're telling the truth. Okay.

154
00:08:24,963 --> 00:08:27,799
I can tell. I won't let you down.

155
00:08:27,882 --> 00:08:29,175
Good.

156
00:08:29,509 --> 00:08:30,510
Thanks.

157
00:08:33,388 --> 00:08:36,433
Nice. That was slick. What are you doing for lunch?

158
00:08:36,516 --> 00:08:37,660
I don't know. I'm probably just gonna eat

159
00:08:37,684 --> 00:08:39,602
my ham and cheese sandwich in the break room.

160
00:08:39,686 --> 00:08:41,438
Oh, nonsense, no way. No.

161
00:08:41,521 --> 00:08:44,899
Why don't I take you out to lunch? My treat.

162
00:08:44,983 --> 00:08:46,651
No. That's all right. Thank you, though.

163
00:08:46,735 --> 00:08:49,380
It's... I gotta do some cleaning, I should probably stick around here.

164
00:08:49,404 --> 00:08:50,655
Hey, you know what we could do?

165
00:08:50,739 --> 00:08:52,466
We could spread out a blanket in the break room,

166
00:08:52,490 --> 00:08:54,701
have a little picnic, order some 'za.

167
00:08:56,286 --> 00:08:57,704
Talk about you know who.

168
00:08:57,787 --> 00:08:59,122
Oh, no.

169
00:08:59,330 --> 00:09:02,000
You know what? Let's go out. That was a good idea. Let's go out.

170
00:09:02,083 --> 00:09:03,668
I know just the place.

171
00:09:06,755 --> 00:09:10,884
Oh, man. You should order milk. Get it?

172
00:09:12,427 --> 00:09:14,054
Why do I like Hooters?

173
00:09:15,055 --> 00:09:19,267
Well, I will give you two reasons. The boobs and the hot wings.

174
00:09:22,854 --> 00:09:25,398
Here we go, here we go. Bogey at 3:00.

175
00:09:25,482 --> 00:09:27,609
Hi. Hey, I'm Dana, welcome to Hooters.

176
00:09:27,692 --> 00:09:31,154
We're not worthy, we're not worthy!

177
00:09:31,946 --> 00:09:36,785
Hello, Dana. I am Michael and this is Jim.

178
00:09:36,868 --> 00:09:39,871
And we are brothers. No. We're not brothers.

179
00:09:39,954 --> 00:09:41,831
I'm his boss, actually, and I treat him well.

180
00:09:41,915 --> 00:09:44,375
I'm taking him out to lunch because I can afford it.

181
00:09:44,459 --> 00:09:45,960
And he can have whatever he wants.

182
00:09:46,044 --> 00:09:47,480
Could I just have the ham and cheese sandwich?

183
00:09:47,504 --> 00:09:48,505
Great. Thanks.

184
00:09:48,588 --> 00:09:51,466
And for you? Tell me, Dana. How is your chicken breast?

185
00:09:51,591 --> 00:09:54,427
Oh, it's great. It's served with our world-famous wing sauce.

186
00:09:54,511 --> 00:09:55,970
Sounds yummy.

187
00:09:56,054 --> 00:09:59,557
I will have a chicken breast, hold the chicken.

188
00:10:01,351 --> 00:10:03,228
Is that what you really want?

189
00:10:06,397 --> 00:10:09,150
No, I'm gonna have the gourmet hot dog. Great.

190
00:10:14,614 --> 00:10:17,325
Who took all the black ones? That's a communal bowl.

191
00:10:17,408 --> 00:10:20,036
So, how did Oscar sound when he called in?

192
00:10:20,161 --> 00:10:23,081
Sick. Like lots of sniffling, I don't know.

193
00:10:23,164 --> 00:10:24,457
Sniffling, how?

194
00:10:25,917 --> 00:10:27,603
How many different ways are there to sniffle?

195
00:10:27,627 --> 00:10:28,837
Three.

196
00:10:29,587 --> 00:10:31,297
Okay, it was the second one.

197
00:10:31,381 --> 00:10:35,051
Okay, good, thank you. That wasn't so hard, now, was it?

198
00:10:40,181 --> 00:10:42,016
What do you like best about Pam?

199
00:10:42,100 --> 00:10:44,018
Oh, I really don't want to talk about it.

200
00:10:44,102 --> 00:10:46,229
Is it her legs, her boobs, her...

201
00:10:47,605 --> 00:10:49,816
She's easy to talk to, I guess.

202
00:10:50,400 --> 00:10:52,402
And, uh, she's got a really good sense of humor.

203
00:10:52,485 --> 00:10:55,321
Really? Never gets any of my jokes.

204
00:10:56,906 --> 00:10:59,534
What about you? Her boobs, definitely.

205
00:10:59,617 --> 00:11:02,203
Wow. That's not what I meant.

206
00:11:02,287 --> 00:11:03,621
Here you go. Oh, thank you.

207
00:11:03,705 --> 00:11:06,374
And I understand we have a birthday today!

208
00:11:06,457 --> 00:11:08,835
Oh, happy birthday, Jim!

209
00:11:08,918 --> 00:11:10,628
Ready, girls? Front side!

210
00:11:10,712 --> 00:11:13,631
<i>You put your front side in You put your front side out</i>

211
00:11:13,715 --> 00:11:16,676
<i>You put your front side in And you shake it all about</i>

212
00:11:16,759 --> 00:11:19,679
<i>You do the hokey-pokey And you turn yourself around</i>

213
00:11:19,762 --> 00:11:21,431
<i>That's what it's all about!</i>

214
00:11:21,514 --> 00:11:24,267
Thank you. Oh, yeah!

215
00:11:24,350 --> 00:11:25,768
Thanks. Thanks, Dana.

216
00:11:25,852 --> 00:11:27,604
Thank you very much!

217
00:11:30,273 --> 00:11:31,274
There you go.

218
00:11:31,357 --> 00:11:32,817
Hilarious. Hey!

219
00:11:33,401 --> 00:11:37,363
What did you guys talk about? Just, you know, politics, literature.

220
00:11:38,781 --> 00:11:39,908
I hate you.

221
00:11:41,868 --> 00:11:43,369
Quick Oscar update.

222
00:11:43,453 --> 00:11:45,639
I have conducted interviews with everyone in the office...

223
00:11:45,663 --> 00:11:47,224
Just go to his house and see if he's sick.

224
00:11:47,248 --> 00:11:49,751
I could have done this investigation in, like, 20 minutes.

225
00:11:49,834 --> 00:11:51,920
Including prep time? Just do it.

226
00:11:57,508 --> 00:12:00,720
<i>If I had to, I could clean out my desk in five seconds,</i>

227
00:12:01,012 --> 00:12:03,556
and nobody would ever know I had ever been here.

228
00:12:04,849 --> 00:12:06,309
And I'd forget, too.

229
00:12:17,904 --> 00:12:19,155
Expense this.

230
00:12:19,656 --> 00:12:24,285
Michael, is that a wig? No, it's...

231
00:12:24,619 --> 00:12:26,371
I wear it like that sometimes.

232
00:12:26,454 --> 00:12:28,414
Is that a wig? No.

233
00:12:28,498 --> 00:12:31,334
This is from Hooters. Yeah. It's a business lunch.

234
00:12:31,417 --> 00:12:35,213
Did Toby approve this? No, he did not. I don't need his permission.

235
00:12:35,672 --> 00:12:37,465
You just got your corporate credit card back.

236
00:12:37,548 --> 00:12:39,342
You really want me to take it away again?

237
00:12:39,425 --> 00:12:40,760
It's ridiculous.

238
00:12:40,843 --> 00:12:44,889
They took my card away because I spent 80 bucks at a magic shop.

239
00:12:44,973 --> 00:12:48,017
What they don't understand is that I bought the stuff

240
00:12:48,101 --> 00:12:52,146
to impress potential clients, so business related. Right?

241
00:12:52,313 --> 00:12:55,275
I put a cigarette through a freaking quarter,

242
00:12:55,650 --> 00:12:58,569
and you know what, Toby, they almost bought from us.

243
00:12:58,653 --> 00:12:59,862
I'm not processing this.

244
00:12:59,946 --> 00:13:03,032
Look, Jim needed a relaxing lunch.

245
00:13:03,116 --> 00:13:06,369
He has been depressed and it has been affecting his productivity.

246
00:13:06,452 --> 00:13:09,038
How is that not work-related? He seems fine to me.

247
00:13:09,122 --> 00:13:10,957
You're not his friend, you don't know.

248
00:13:11,040 --> 00:13:13,960
He is in love with a girl he works with who is engaged,

249
00:13:14,043 --> 00:13:16,170
so just cut me some slack. Please?

250
00:13:16,254 --> 00:13:17,380
Pam?

251
00:13:26,556 --> 00:13:29,309
Angela, who would you choose? Jim or Roy?

252
